1
00:02:53,142 --> 00:02:59,142
He’s having the worst day of his life… Over and over again.

2
00:05:46,285 --> 00:05:52,285
Groundhog Day is a romance, fantasy, comedy film directed by Harold Ramis.

3
00:08:39,428 --> 00:08:45,428
A narcissistic TV weatherman, along with his attractive-but-distant producer, and his mawkish cameraman, is sent to report on
Groundhog Day in the small town of Punxsutawney, where he finds himself repeating the same day over and over.

4
00:11:32,571 --> 00:11:38,571
Phil Connors, played by Bill Murray.

5
00:14:25,714 --> 00:14:31,714
Rita Hanson, played by Andie MacDowell.

6
00:17:18,857 --> 00:17:24,857
Larry, played by Chris Elliott.

7
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ned Ryerson, played by Stephen Tobolowsky.

8
00:23:05,142 --> 00:23:11,142
Buster Green, played by Brian Doyle-Murray.

9
00:25:58,285 --> 00:26:04,285
Nancy Taylor, played by Marita Geraghty.

10
00:28:51,428 --> 00:28:57,428
Groundhog Day is a 1993 American fantasy and romantic comedy film directed
by Harold Ramis from a screenplay by him and Danny Rubin.

11
00:31:44,571 --> 00:31:50,571
Starring Bill Murray, Andie MacDowell, and Chris Elliott, it tells the story of a cynical television weatherman covering the annual
Groundhog Day event in Punxsutawney, Pennsylvania, who becomes trapped in a time loop, forcing him to relive February 2 repeatedly.

12
00:34:37,714 --> 00:34:43,714
The film also features Stephen Tobolowsky, Brian Doyle-Murray, Marita Geraghty, Angela
Paton, Rick Ducommun, Rick Overton, and Robin Duke in supporting roles.

13
00:37:30,857 --> 00:37:36,857
Rubin conceived Groundhog Day in the early 1990s.

14
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
He wrote it as a spec script to gain meetings with producers for other work.

15
00:43:17,142 --> 00:43:23,142
It eventually came to the attention of Ramis, who worked with Rubin to make his idea less
dark in tone and more palatable to a general audience by enhancing the comedy.

16
00:46:10,285 --> 00:46:16,285
Murray clashed with Ramis over the script; he wanted to focus on the
philosophical elements, whereas Ramis concentrated on the comedic aspects.

17
00:49:03,428 --> 00:49:09,428
Principal photography took place from March to June 1992,
almost entirely in Woodstock, Illinois.

18
00:51:56,571 --> 00:52:02,571
Filming was difficult, in part because of bitterly cold weather but also
because of the ongoing conflict between Ramis and Murray.

19
00:54:49,714 --> 00:54:55,714
Groundhog Day premiered at the Fox Village Theatre on February 4, 1993
and was released by Columbia Pictures on February 12.

20
00:57:42,857 --> 00:57:48,857
Earning over $105 million, it became one of the year's highest-grossing films.

21
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
It also received generally positive reviews.

22
01:03:29,142 --> 01:03:35,142
Critics praised the melding of sentimental and cynical moments,
and the philosophical message beneath the comedy.

23
01:06:22,285 --> 01:06:28,285
It was nominated for multiple awards and won a BAFTA
Award for Best Original Screenplay.

24
01:09:15,428 --> 01:09:21,428
The film marked the end of Murray and Ramis's longtime collaborative partnership,
which had produced films like Caddyshack (1980) and Ghostbusters (1984).

25
01:12:08,571 --> 01:12:14,571
After filming ended, the pair did not speak to each other
until shortly before Ramis's death in 2014.

26
01:15:01,714 --> 01:15:07,714
The film was a showcase for Murray; he had previously been seen primarily as a comic actor,
and his performance led to more serious roles in critically acclaimed films.

27
01:17:54,857 --> 01:18:00,857
In the years since its release, the film has grown in esteem; it is often considered
among the greatest films of the 1990s and one of the greatest comedy films.

28
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
It has also had a significant effect on popular culture: the term Groundhog Day, meaning a
monotonous, unpleasant, and repetitive situation, has become part of the English lexicon.

29
01:23:41,142 --> 01:23:47,142
Buddhist, Christian, and Jewish scholars have
analyzed the film as a religious allegory.

30
01:26:34,285 --> 01:26:40,285
Groundhog Day is also credited with having ushered in mainstream acceptance of comedy
films with fantasy-genre elements, and popularizing time loop narratives.

31
01:29:27,428 --> 01:29:33,428
In 2006, the United States Library of Congress selected the film
for preservation in the National Film Registry.

32
01:32:20,571 --> 01:32:26,571
Groundhog Day was adapted into a 2016 musical, and inspired a 2019
video game sequel, Groundhog Day: Like Father Like Son.

33
01:35:13,714 --> 01:35:19,714
The film explores themes of deja vu, groundhog, weather
forecast, telecaster, pennsylvania, usa.

34
01:38:06,857 --> 01:38:12,857
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
